# Ame development USB access for a non-root console user.
#
# Two nodes matter:
#   1. the CDC ACM serial port used by `screen` and scripts/anne/usb-input.py
#   2. the raw USB device node, needed by the vendor bulk interface (pyusb)
#
# Matched on VID/PID rather than ttyACM<N> or bus numbers: Ame re-enumerates
# after every boot and the node index changes.
#
# The tty rule deliberately uses ATTR{}, not ATTRS{}. ATTRS{} walks up the
# device chain and matches the FIRST ancestor carrying those attributes, which
# for a tty is the xHCI host controller (1d6b:"xHCI Host Controller") - so an
# ATTRS{idVendor}=="1209" test silently never matches and the rule appears to
# do nothing even though `udevadm test` shows it being read. The tty device
# itself already carries ID_VENDOR_ID/ID_MODEL_ID from its parent, so plain
# ATTR{} on those properties is both correct and cheaper.
#
# Install:  sudo install -m 0644 scripts/anne/udev/99-ame-serial.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#           sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#           (then re-plug, or sudo udevadm trigger --action=add)
#
# Replace OWNER with your own login if it is not lucas.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", KERNEL=="ttyACM[0-9]*", ATTR{idVendor}=="1209", ATTR{idProduct}=="0001", OWNER="lucas", MODE="0600", SYMLINK+="ame"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="1209", ATTR{idProduct}=="0001", OWNER="lucas", MODE="0600"
